The original does a linear scan over the whole `mesgs` table on every lookup. This version builds a 64K-entry index once and then answers each lookup with a single array read.

- **Safe to cache:** the index is built from the constant `mesgs` table, so it does not depend on any global mutable state.
- **Thread-safe setup:** it lives in a function-local static, which C++ initializes only once even with concurrent callers.
- **Same results:** the first matching entry still wins, as in the original scan. A missing number still returns `NULL`.

```cpp
const Profile::MESG* Profile::GetMesg(const FIT_UINT16 num)
{
    struct Index
    {
        FIT_UINT16 idx[65536];
        Index()
        {
            for (int k = 0; k < 65536; k++)
                idx[k] = 0xFFFF;
            for (int i = 0; i < MESGS; i++)
            {
                FIT_UINT16 n = mesgs[i].num;
                if (idx[n] == 0xFFFF)
                    idx[n] = (FIT_UINT16)i;
            }
        }
    };
    static const Index* const index = new Index();

    const FIT_UINT16 i = index->idx[num];
    if (i == 0xFFFF)
        return NULL;
    return &mesgs[i];
}
```